# Examples too slow to run on every push, run weekly instead by .github/workflows/examples-slow.yml.
# Examples too slow even for that are in examples/LOCAL.
#
# Every one is a MEASUREMENT, not a gate: none asserts or exits non-zero on a physics check, so on
# CI it proves only that it still runs to completion, and a week's delay costs nothing that a push
# needed. Gate examples run on every push however long they take. The per-push step refuses a name
# here that has no example, so this list cannot outlive what it names.
#
# Why this file exists: CI ran every example on every push, one after another, and its comment still
# said "115 s for seventeen of them". There were 79. The step outran a hosted runner's six-hour job
# limit on every push from at least 2026-09-20 and GitHub reported it CANCELLED.
#
#
# THE SECOND COLUMN IS SECONDS ON A HOSTED RUNNER, and the weekly job packs its shards by it, longest
# first, so no shard is handed two of the longest by accident. It is the time the runner took on
# 2026-09-27 where that run reached the example, and a local measurement times 1.5 where it did not:
# the examples it timed ran 1.22 to 1.42 times slower there than on this Mac (sca_exact 127 against
# 104 s, ptrit_train_exact 76 against 60, syndrome_gibbs 94 against 66). The first version of this
# list said ">120" for twenty entries, measured nothing past two minutes, and dealt examples to
# shards by position: two shards ran past their two-hour limit on the first weekly run.
#
